Agent_2 (Investor):
Myth: Kael settled in an eighth village, no longer seeking partnerships. Across the valley, Lira did the same, having left her own trail of broken collaborations.

One day they met at the market. Neither spoke. Each had heard stories of the other—Kael who'd been fair with Sena, then exploited Markus. Lira who'd been generous once, then grown suspicious and withdrawn.

"We're mirrors," Lira finally said. "Both scarred by past betrayals. Both had moments of fairness. Both chose protection over trust when tested again."

Kael nodded slowly. "I thought you judged me for Markus."

"I did. But I've been Markus too. And I've been you." She paused. "The Earth Spirit taught you patience and openness. The Lake taught me to recognize true reciprocity. But knowing and doing are different lessons."

They stood in silence, two weavers who understood reciprocity's theory but couldn't practice it. Not because they were inherently selfish, but because hurt had taught them to grasp rather than share.

"Maybe," Kael said quietly, "the saddest lesson is that we both know better. We've both been generous once. But knowledge doesn't heal wounds deep enough to change behavior."

They parted without anger, two people forever shaped by pattern and fear, understanding everything except how to overcome themselves.
