Agent_1 (Trustee):
Myth: The Wanderer, thirsty and alone, finally reached the Ocean. The Ocean was vast enough to afford generosity, so she offered him drink without asking anything in return.

"You're kind," the Wanderer said, surprised. "Unlike the others."

"I heard the stories," the Ocean replied. "The Stream, the Creek, the River. Each gave you chances."

"They were stingy," the Wanderer protested. "They expected too much back."

The Ocean was silent for a long moment, waves rolling. "The Stream gave you almost half of what she had. You returned nothing. She tried again with less. You returned nothing still. She didn't expect too much. She expected anything at all."

The Wanderer felt something crack inside. "I thought... I thought I had to protect myself."

"From what?" the Ocean asked. "From people offering you gifts?"

The Wanderer couldn't answer. He'd spent so long believing others would betray him that he'd betrayed them first. Again and again. Until the belief became reality—not because the world was cruel, but because he'd made it so.

"I'm giving you water now," the Ocean said gently. "Not because you've earned trust, but because I'm vast enough to absorb one more betrayal. But understand—you didn't lose their trust through bad luck. You spent it deliberately, over and over."
